cff-version: 1.2.0

message: "If you use this project, please cite it using these metadata."

type: software

title: "Analysis of Geomagnetic Activity and Reported Aurora Sightings Using Python and Power BI"

authors:
  - family-names: "MOHAMED KASIM"
    given-names: "MOHAMED AYAS"
    affiliation: "Universidad Autónoma de Nuevo León"

abstract: >-
  A reproducible scientific computing project examining the relationship
  between geomagnetic activity and citizen-reported aurora sightings in 2024.
  Planetary Kp observations from the GFZ Helmholtz Centre for Geosciences
  are analyzed alongside Aurorasaurus reports, with NASA DONKI geomagnetic
  storm-event records providing supporting comparisons. An October 2026
  Kp analysis is retained as an additional case study. The project uses
  scientific APIs, Python data processing, structured data storage, and
  Power BI for visualization and validation.

repository-code: "https://github.com/mohamedayas16/Semester_2_CS_2026"

keywords:
  - scientific computing
  - geomagnetic activity
  - Kp index
